  "title": "Myanmar Diarrhoea Outbreak: Hundreds Hospitalised as Flooding Raises Health Concerns",
  "summary": "A diarrhoea outbreak in Yangon has led to 182 hospital admissions as Myanmar faces monsoon flooding, contaminated water risks and an ongoing humanitarian crisis. Myanmar Faces Growing Diarrhoea Outbreak in Yangon Myanmar is facing a significant public health concern after a sharp increase in acute diarrhoea cases was reported in Yangon, the country's largest city. The outbreak comes during the annual monsoon season, when heavy rainfall and flooding can increase the risk of waterborne diseases",
